<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vega of Granada</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vega of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> is the fertile plain around the city of Granada in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, watered by the Genil river and its tributaries. Under the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> its dense network of irrigation channels supported cereals, fruit, vegetables and mulberry trees for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, feeding the capital. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a> Castilian armies repeatedly ravaged it to weaken the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vega-of-granada.jpg" alt="Vega of Granada" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LocationVega_de_Granada.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
